# Touchstone-86, tour: the menu, test 01 passing, identity (BB 86), the static test counting for a second, the core's questions (BE 07).
# For DS2 (HI on the silk): set CONST ROLE = 2 in Touchstone.bas.
# Written by TTLSim's TouchstoneRomTests from tstrom.asm on Ida's 8086 core at 4 MHz; not edited by hand.
# Power-on at 0; the CPU leaves reset at 250 ms.
THING OledThing
0.000 B=C3
250.024 B=01
346.221 B=A1
346.510 B=C1
446.230 B=02
546.235 B=03
646.240 B=04
746.245 B=05
846.250 B=06
946.255 B=07
1046.260 B=08
1146.265 B=09
1246.270 B=0A
1346.275 B=0B
1446.272 B=AB
1446.406 B=BB
1546.288 B=0C
1646.285 B=AC
2746.322 B=CC
2846.298 B=0D
2946.303 B=0E
3046.300 B=AE
3046.777 B=BE
END 3547.000
